            <ArticleTitle>[Methotrexate may be a useful corticosteroid reducing treatment of severe asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">V10130598</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asthma is a chronic airway disease affecting many people worldwide. Less than 1% suffers from difficult-to-treat asthma and requires systemic corticosteroid treatment to achieve symptom control. The therapeutic options for these patients are limited and often we have to accept a lesser degree of symptom control. Methotrexate has been evaluated in 13 studies, where the mean corticosteroid dose reduction was 35%. Despite the adverse effects, we find that methotrexate may be a useful treatment of severe asthma in certain patients under close observation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
